- "[Echinacea]"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6095 (mes)
- "What do you not understand?"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6096 (mes)
- "Nothing good can come out of this if it's released to the public."
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6097 (mes)
- "Can't you see?"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6098 (mes)
- "[Echinacea]"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6099 (mes)
- "Arunafeltz has replaced their leaders with the moderates just recently."
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6100 (mes)
- "Shoving the remnants of the radicals in front of them is extremely dangerous."
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6101 (mes)
- "[Echinacea]"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6102 (mes)
- "We've finally made a truce with them."
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6103 (mes)
- "Their sins will not be forgiven, but we won't make a stupid attempt to get revenge and end up shedding more blood!"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6104 (mes)
- "[Echinacea]"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6105 (mes)
- "Let the politicians do their job."
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6106 (mes)
- "I assure you they won't lead us to the worst case scenario. That's what you're worried about, right?"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6107 (mes)
- "[Echinacea]"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6108 (mes)
- "No, wait.. Do you..?"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6109 (mes)
- "Do you want us to wage war against Arunafeltz over this?!"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6110 (mes)
- "[Echinacea]"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6111 (mes)
- "Let me ask you to forget the past and focus on the present."
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6112 (mes)
- "For everyone's sake, please just look toward the future and move forward."
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6113 (mes)
- "[Echinacea]"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6114 (mes)
- "We won't do anything that you'd morally oppose."
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6115 (mes)
- "You believe in peace, don't you?"
+ ""
#: npc/quests/quests_13_1.txt#6116 (mes)
- "Tell him that I'm grateful for these sweet potatoes, anyway.."
