#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#868 (npctalk)
- "I had nothing to do with it."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#869 (npctalk)
- "Mojo#ilgf"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#870 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#871 (mes)
- "Some mages decided to erect an ivory tower of their own. They searched everywhere in the continent and settled on the ground above these catacombs."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#872 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#873 (mes)
- "That was the beginning of the tragedy."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#875 (npctalk)
- "Oh geez, here it goes again."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#876 (npctalk)
- "Mojo#ilgf"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#877 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#878 (mes)
- "It's been said all mammals have curiosity that rivals their appetite, but mages... are the worst. "
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#879 (npctalk)
- "Enough with the lecturing. Get to the point already."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#880 (npctalk)
- "Mojo#ilgf"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#881 (npctalk)
- "Everything has a cause and effect. How can you expect the adventurer to understand what this is about without knowing the cause?"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#882 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#883 (mes)
- "Anyway, these mages, after they built the Geffen Tower, took notice of the blasphemous creatures that sometimes appeared in the catacombs."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#884 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#885 (mes)
- "They conducted various experiments to understand the special energy that reanimated the dead."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#886 (npctalk)
- "They were just studying."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#887 (npctalk)
- "Mojo#ilgf"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#888 (npctalk)
- "Just studying? They could've turned the entire continent into an unholy breeding ground!"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#889 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#890 (mes)
- "And as if that wasn't enough, those mages used their magic and replicated the reanimating process."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#891 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#892 (mes)
- "That went horribly wrong. The special energy that surrounded the catacombs exploded, bringing back all the dead buried in them."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#893 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#894 (mes)
- "Those arrogant mages crossed the line! They tried to play God!"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#896 (mes)
- "[Mojo]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#897 (mes)
- "Hey, I'm one of them, and I'm not going to let you talk bad about my predecessors like that!"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#898 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#899 (mes)
- "How am I defaming them when I'm only telling the truth?"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#900 (npctalk)
- "It's not telling the truth when you're only telling it from your point of view!"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#901 (npctalk)
- "Mojo#ilgf"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#902 (mes)
- "[Grimm]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#903 (mes)
