#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2950 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2951 (mes)
- "She still hasn't forgiven me. But I did what I had to do."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2952 (select)
- "There must be some misunderstanding."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2953 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2954 (mes)
- "I needed humans to survive. I hid among them and hunted them whenever I needed."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2955 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2956 (mes)
- "One day, people from the Church found me. They were bent on killing me in the name of justice."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2957 (npctalk)
- "They were persistent."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2958 (npctalk)
- "King#ilgf01"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2959 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2960 (mes)
- "I was gravely injured by them, and somehow I ended up in this place full of death and mysterious energy."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2961 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2962 (mes)
- "I thought I was going to die here, but then Lady Luck finally turned her gaze upon me."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2963 (npctalk)
- "Somebody please shut him up. I hate this story."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2964 (npctalk)
- "King#ilgf01"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2965 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2966 (mes)
- "Bomi saved me. She fed me her blood, so I could regain my strength. I'm not a living being, but that day, she gave me new life."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2967 (mes)
- "[Jojo]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2968 (mes)
- "Why didn't you leave afterward?"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2969 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2970 (mes)
- "Even though Bomi was a strong woman, her body was failing her. It pained me to see her waste away day by day. I offered her eternal life, and she rejected it."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2971 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2972 (mes)
- "I stayed because I wanted to be there for her when she died as a human."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2973 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2974 (mes)
- "For the first time in my long existence, I really thought about humans, and what made them who they were. They also have this impulse to help others, expecting nothing in return."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2975 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2976 (mes)
- "I'd learned about them through Bomi. What I'd learned didn't make sense, and I didn't really understand it."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2977 (mes)
- "[Dracula]"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2978 (mes)
- "But it was different from what I previously thought of humans. I was starting to understand them."
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2979 (npctalk)
- "Why? What good would understanding them do you?"
+ ""
#: npc/re/quests/quests_illusion_dungeons.txt#2980 (npctalk)
